What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/10000000.clock-controller/dcm_state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only MT6580 clock-driver CPU/bus DCM diagnostics. owned=1
		means the configured driver applied CPU Mode 1 and infra/peri
		policy. valid=1 means all owned control bits currently match it.
		applies counts initial/resume-noirq policy applications;
		resume_fixes counts mismatches repaired at resume-noirq. Deep
		finisher pause/restores have separate counters in the SPM state
		attribute; they are not late repair applications.

		The six before/current words are ordered INFRACFG offsets
		0x14/0x10/0xa00 and TOPCKGEN 0x20/0x28/0x2c. before is the
		initial firmware snapshot. current is read under the shared
		clock lock; unrelated bits may legitimately change with other
		clock consumers. With owned=0 no policy is promised; zero words
		without an acquired mapping are not measured register values.

		This reports control bits, not time spent gated or electrical
		power consumption. It exposes no write or runtime mode switch.
